## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Framework choice:** The plan uses **Vite + React** (client-side SPA). This means no server, no database — everything runs in the browser with localStorage for persistence. If you later want cloud sync or sharing lessons via URL, we'd add a lightweight backend. Is this acceptable for the initial version?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **GSAP licensing:** GSAP is free for personal/educational use. The free tier includes timeline, SVG transforms, and all core features we need. The premium `MorphSVGPlugin` (for true path morphing) requires a paid license — we can work around this with opacity-based transitions and position animations instead. Acceptable?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Mafs vs custom canvas:** Mafs provides excellent out-of-the-box interactive 2D math (draggable points, function plotting, vectors). The tradeoff is that we depend on their component API. If we need extreme custom animation control, we could use raw SVG + GSAP instead, but this would require significantly more work. Recommendation: start with Mafs, eject to raw SVG only for specific animations Mafs can't handle.

## Open Questions

> [!WARNING]
> **Question 1:** For the AI input flow, do you want to be able to paste JSON directly into the app, or would you also want a "chat-like" interface where you can describe what you want and the app calls an AI API (e.g., Gemini/Claude) to generate the lesson JSON automatically?

> [!WARNING]
> **Question 2:** Do you want 3D visualisation support in v1 (e.g., 3D vectors, surfaces, rotations)? This would add significant complexity (MathBox/Three.js integration) and I'd recommend deferring to v2.

> [!WARNING]
> **Question 3:** For the matrix renderer — do you want matrices to be a separate "full-screen" element (like they'd be in their own scene), or should they coexist alongside a coordinate plane (e.g., showing a matrix transformation AND its geometric effect side by side)?

> [!WARNING]
> **Question 4:** Audio narration — would you eventually want text-to-speech for the narration text, or is text-only display sufficient?

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Testing
- JSON schema validation unit tests (valid/invalid lesson fixtures)
- Equation parser unit tests (tagged format extraction)
- Animation factory unit tests (correct GSAP timeline construction)
- `npm run build` — verifies no TypeScript errors

### Visual Testing
- Load each of the 7 baseline test cases in the browser
- Verify via browser session recordings:
  - Equations render correctly with colour coding
  - Morph animations move terms smoothly without overlap
  - Canvas objects appear in correct positions with correct colours
  - Interactive elements (sliders, drag) work as expected
  - Transport controls (play/pause/step/speed) function correctly
  - Cross-referencing (hover equation term highlights graph element) works
- Verify the JSON importer accepts valid JSON and rejects invalid JSON with helpful error messages

### Manual Testing
- Test all 7 lessons end-to-end in auto-play mode
- Test stepping through each lesson manually
- Test speed control at all settings
- Test importing a custom lesson JSON
- Verify the AI prompt template produces valid JSON when given to an AI
